With maps, instead of just having a seen/unseen state, we also partilaly darken any that are outside of a given radius from the player, not renderering anything outside of that range.
It might be nice to have that visibility taper out a few cells

Enemies should not spawn within a certain radius of the player (maybe five cells or so)

No enemies should ever spawn (or respawn) within the player's view range, except on the initial drawing of the map.

Give player a "sight" skill, and also add an optional "visibility" value on levels.  Perhaps a 0-1 value that can be multiplied by the player's sight skill to get their actual range of view. Also consider things like potions that temporarily boost sight.

As suggested, we should loosen up on stopping keyboard events.  So far the game is playable with the mouse - we may not need the keyboard at all.
